# "oldfail": the newest failure (100) is older than 30 COMPLETED groups, so it
# lies beyond the finished block's default cap of 25 rows in COMPACT.  106, the
# group the cap cuts first, is a 3-task array: when the failure takes the last
# row, 106 moves into "+N more" with its 3 jobs, so "+8 more" (not 6) tells a
# shifted block from one where the failure merely overwrote that row.
@include ../_common/sacct-defaults
